# How the village's events are told.
#
#   rule-title: sentence          one sentence per firing of that rule
#   chain a + b within N: ...     two firings within N weeks sharing a person,
#                                 told once; {1.X} is a's X, {2.X} is b's X
#   silent <pattern>              never read this edge type out in a fallback
#   rule-title:                   (nothing after the colon) say nothing at all
#
# {A} is a name. {A:he} {A:him} {A:his} {A:man} {A:son} {A:husband} {A:father}
# pick the word by gender; {A:He} capitalises it. A week node reads as a
# calendar phrase: "late March", "early June of the following year".
# A rule with no line here has its inserted edges read out plainly, minus the
# silent ones.

# --- what matters ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `important <rule> <rule> ...`: with --important only these are told (a
# released or cancelled schedule counts under its rule). Courtship, grudges
# and pregnancies are the weather; these are the events.

important they-get-engaged the-vows-are-said the-betrothed-mourns
important the-heads-make-a-match the-heads-make-peace-with-a-match the-church-forbids-the-match
important she-runs-off-with-her-lover he-runs-off-with-his-lover
important the-jilted-man-plots-against-the-lover the-jilted-woman-plots-against-the-lover the-jilted-nurse-a-grudge
important the-feud-claims-a-target the-feud-burns-out the-houses-take-the-blood-price
# Friendships FORMING are weather - hundreds a year in a large world. What
# friends do is the story.
important a-friend-is-drawn-into-the-plot a-friend-warns-his-friend
important a-friend-turns-on-a-killer a-betrayed-friendship-is-over a-friend-avenges-a-friend
important the-kin-name-a-price the-blood-price-is-paid the-price-is-refused
important he-plots-against-the-groom she-plots-against-the-bride he-covets-another-mans-wife she-covets-another-womans-husband
important the-plotter-finds-an-accomplice a-lover-is-drawn-into-the-plot the-accomplice-turns the-betrayed-man-learns-of-it
important the-warned-strike-first poison a-knife-in-the-dark the-river the-moment-passes
important blood-for-blood a-father-avenges-his-son the-widow-swears-vengeance a-kinsman-takes-up-the-blood-debt
important the-widow-learns-who-killed-him she-dies-in-childbed
important the-eavesdropper-warns-the-victim the-eavesdropper-denounces-a-traitor
important the-crown-outlaws-the-traitor an-outlaw-is-hunted-down the-outlaw-is-pardoned
important the-heir-is-named the-heir-takes-the-throne a-sworn-house-seizes-the-throne the-pretender-seizes-the-throne
# Overhearing and declaring are weather at scale - tens of thousands a year.
# What a listener DOES with what he heard is the story.
important a-claimant-plots-against-the-king the-crown-is-vacant
important the-witness-asks-for-silence the-blackmail-is-paid the-blackmailer-is-silenced
important old-age a-sudden-illness death-comes the-house-passes-to-a-son the-house-passes-to-a-kinsman
important a-killer-confesses the-priest-breaks-the-seal the-priest-tells-the-son the-unshriven-are-refused-burial
important the-suspicion-is-said-aloud the-houses-fall-out-over-an-accusation the-accused-strikes-back
important the-note-comes-due a-ruined-house-marries-down a-ruined-man-turns-on-his-creditor

# --- how much each thing counts ----------------------------------------------
#
# `weight N <rule> ...` ranks a firing when a month has more events than the
# chronicle has room to tell at length. Without a line, an `important` rule is
# worth 10 and everything else 1. A death and a wedding outrank a betrothal;
# a betrothal outranks a friendship.

weight 40 death-comes old-age a-sudden-illness a-child-sickens she-dies-in-childbed
weight 40 released:poison released:a-knife-in-the-dark released:the-river
weight 38 an-outlaw-is-hunted-down
weight 36 the-vows-are-said
weight 34 the-heir-takes-the-throne a-sworn-house-seizes-the-throne the-pretender-seizes-the-throne the-crown-is-vacant
weight 30 she-runs-off-with-her-lover he-runs-off-with-his-lover
weight 28 the-crown-outlaws-the-traitor the-outlaw-is-pardoned
weight 26 blood-for-blood a-father-avenges-his-son the-widow-swears-vengeance a-kinsman-takes-up-the-blood-debt
weight 26 a-friend-avenges-a-friend the-feud-claims-a-target
weight 24 poison a-knife-in-the-dark the-river
weight 22 the-heads-make-peace-with-a-match the-houses-take-the-blood-price the-feud-burns-out
weight 20 they-get-engaged the-heads-make-a-match the-betrothed-mourns the-heir-is-named
weight 18 he-plots-against-the-groom she-plots-against-the-bride the-blackmailer-is-silenced
weight 16 the-jilted-man-plots-against-the-lover the-jilted-woman-plots-against-the-lover
weight 16 a-claimant-plots-against-the-king the-eavesdropper-denounces-a-traitor
weight 14 the-warned-strike-first the-accomplice-turns a-friend-warns-his-friend a-friend-turns-on-a-killer
weight 14 the-widow-learns-who-killed-him the-kin-name-a-price the-price-is-refused the-blood-price-is-paid
weight 12 a-child-is-born the-house-passes-to-a-son the-house-passes-to-a-kinsman
weight 10 the-plotter-finds-an-accomplice a-friend-is-drawn-into-the-plot a-lover-is-drawn-into-the-plot
weight 10 the-witness-asks-for-silence the-blackmail-is-paid a-thin-wall a-house-backs-the-pretender
weight  8 she-conceives comes-of-age the-jilted-nurse-a-grudge a-betrayed-friendship-is-over
weight  6 the-esteem-is-returned the-feeling-is-returned strangers-take-against-each-other
weight  4 hatred-fades the-moment-passes the-suit-is-rebuffed

# The three new arcs. A confession outranks the penance it earns; a public
# accusation outranks the muttering behind it; the note coming due outranks
# the borrowing that led to it - in each case the consequence is the event
# and the setup is the weather.
weight 30 the-priest-breaks-the-seal the-priest-tells-the-son
weight 26 a-killer-confesses the-unshriven-are-refused-burial
weight 24 the-accused-strikes-back a-ruined-man-turns-on-his-creditor
weight 22 the-houses-fall-out-over-an-accusation the-note-comes-due
weight 20 a-ruined-house-marries-down
weight 16 the-suspicion-is-said-aloud
weight 14 a-new-priest-is-ordained
weight 12 the-priest-sets-a-penance a-penitent-gives-up-his-plot
weight 10 the-penance-is-done
weight  8 suspicion-falls-on-the-other-house a-widow-suspects-the-other-house the-son-looks-for-someone-to-blame
weight  6 the-head-borrows the-debt-is-settled the-suspicion-spreads
weight  4 a-hard-season the-house-recovers

# --- what a dropped event counts as ------------------------------------------
#
# Anything the month has no room to tell at length is counted into its
# category and read out at the end: "Elsewhere that month: two deaths and
# four quarrels." A rule with no category falls under `other`.

category death:      death-comes old-age a-sudden-illness a-child-sickens she-dies-in-childbed
category death:      released:poison released:a-knife-in-the-dark released:the-river an-outlaw-is-hunted-down
category birth:      a-child-is-born she-conceives comes-of-age
category marriage:   they-get-engaged they-set-a-date they-take-their-time they-wait-for-a-better-season
category marriage:   the-vows-are-said the-heads-make-a-match the-heads-make-peace-with-a-match
category marriage:   the-betrothed-mourns the-church-forbids-the-match the-engagement-dies-with-him
category courtship:  the-feeling-is-returned he-notices-her she-notices-him the-suit-is-rebuffed
category friendship: the-esteem-is-returned a-betrayed-friendship-is-over
category quarrel:    strangers-take-against-each-other hatred-fades hatred-poisons-affection
category quarrel:    the-jilted-nurse-a-grudge the-jilted-let-it-go
category plot:       he-plots-against-the-groom she-plots-against-the-bride he-covets-another-mans-wife
category plot:       she-covets-another-womans-husband the-plotter-finds-an-accomplice poison
category plot:       a-knife-in-the-dark the-river the-moment-passes a-lover-is-drawn-into-the-plot
category plot:       the-jilted-man-plots-against-the-lover the-jilted-woman-plots-against-the-lover
category vengeance:  blood-for-blood a-father-avenges-his-son the-widow-swears-vengeance
category vengeance:  a-kinsman-takes-up-the-blood-debt a-friend-avenges-a-friend the-feud-claims-a-target
category vengeance:  the-kin-name-a-price the-blood-price-is-paid the-price-is-refused
category crown:      the-heir-is-named the-heir-takes-the-throne the-crown-is-vacant a-house-backs-the-pretender
category crown:      a-claimant-plots-against-the-king the-crown-outlaws-the-traitor the-outlaw-is-pardoned
category crown:      a-sworn-house-seizes-the-throne the-pretender-seizes-the-throne

category church:    a-killer-confesses the-priest-sets-a-penance a-penitent-gives-up-his-plot
category church:    the-penance-is-done the-priest-breaks-the-seal the-priest-tells-the-son
category church:    the-unshriven-are-refused-burial a-new-priest-is-ordained
category suspicion: suspicion-falls-on-the-other-house a-widow-suspects-the-other-house
category suspicion: the-son-looks-for-someone-to-blame the-suspicion-spreads the-suspicion-is-said-aloud
category suspicion: the-houses-fall-out-over-an-accusation the-accused-strikes-back
category silver:    a-hard-season the-head-borrows the-debt-is-settled the-note-comes-due
category silver:    a-ruined-house-marries-down a-ruined-man-turns-on-his-creditor the-house-recovers

summary death:      a death / {n} deaths
summary birth:      a birth / {n} births
summary marriage:   a match made / {n} matches made
summary courtship:  a courtship begun / {n} courtships begun
summary friendship: a friendship / {n} friendships
summary quarrel:    a quarrel / {n} quarrels
summary plot:       a plot laid / {n} plots laid
summary vengeance:  a debt of blood / {n} debts of blood
summary crown:      a move on the crown / {n} moves on the crown
summary church:     a matter for the priest / {n} matters for the priest
summary suspicion:  a suspicion voiced / {n} suspicions voiced
summary silver:     a debt / {n} debts
summary other:      one smaller matter / {n} smaller matters

# --- words the prose reaches for ---------------------------------------------
#
# `<name>` in any sentence here, or in a dialogue line, expands to one of the
# alternatives. `*N` weights one. The choice is a hash of the seed and the
# firing, so a run repeats exactly and two firings of one rule in one month do
# not reach for the same word.

sub then:    Then  *3 | Soon after,  | Before the month was out,  | That same month,  | Not long after,

# Used instead of `<then>` when the programme's own rules say the later thing
# could have been brought about by the earlier one, and the two share a
# person. Nothing declares which pairs those are - see ConsequenceGraph.
sub therefore: And so *2 | Which is why | It followed that | The upshot was that | For that reason

# `incidental <pattern>`: a real edge that is nonetheless not a reason to say
# one thing led to another. A plot resolving hands `keeps the peace` back to
# the plotter, which would make every killing in the village the cause of
# every plot that came after it; the same is true of being alive and of
# being grown.
incidental ? keeps the peace
incidental ? is alive
incidental ? is grown
incidental ? is unattached
incidental ? is unmarried
incidental ? lives in ?
incidental ? is of age
sub anger:   fury | a cold rage | something that would not cool | a grudge he would not set down
sub quietly: quietly | without raising his voice | flatly | with no heat at all

