# --- chains: one event, not two ----------------------------------------------
#
# Earlier chains win, and a firing is used by at most one chain.

chain he-notices-her + the-feeling-is-returned within 6:
  {1.A} began to notice {1.B}, and before long {1.B} returned the feeling.

chain she-notices-him + the-feeling-is-returned within 6:
  {1.A} found herself drawn to {1.B}, and {1.B} soon felt the same.

chain they-get-engaged + they-set-a-date within 3:
  {1.A} and {1.B} were engaged, and set their wedding for {2.D'}.

chain they-get-engaged + they-take-their-time within 3:
  {1.A} and {1.B} were engaged, and in no great hurry set their wedding for {2.D'}.

chain they-get-engaged + they-wait-for-a-better-season within 3:
  {1.A} and {1.B} were engaged, and would wait for a better season: the wedding was set for {2.D'}.

chain strangers-take-against-each-other + hatred-fades within 8:
  {1.A} took against {1.B} for a while, then let it go.

chain a-friend-warns-his-friend + the-warned-strike-first within 4:
  {1.X} would not see {1.B} come to harm and told {1.B:him} what {1.C} intended; forewarned, {1.B} resolved to strike first.

chain the-kin-name-a-price + the-blood-price-is-paid within 12:
  {1.X} named a price for {1.C}'s death, and {1.A} paid it.

chain the-kin-name-a-price + the-price-is-refused within 12:
  {1.X} named a price for {1.C}'s death, then would not be paid, and swore {1.A} would answer for it.

chain the-accomplice-turns + the-warned-strike-first within 4:
  {1.X} lost {1.X:his} nerve and warned {1.B} what {1.C} intended; forewarned, {1.B} resolved to strike first.

chain the-widow-learns-who-killed-him + the-widow-swears-vengeance within 4:
  {1.B} learned it was {1.A} who had killed {1.C}, and swore {1.A:he} would pay for it.

chain the-jilted-nurse-a-grudge + the-feud-claims-a-target within 12:
  {1.B} never forgave {1.A}, and with the houses at feud marked {2.Y} for death.

chain the-widow-learns-who-killed-him + the-widow-forgoes-vengeance within 6:
  {1.B} learned it was {1.A} who had killed {1.C}, and hated {1.A:him} for it, but did nothing.

# --- chains for the three new arcs -------------------------------------------
#
# A chain is where the long sentences come from: several firings that are one
# event told once, with the connective tissue written in. A chain only forms
# when every letter the two rules SHARE is bound to the same node, so the
# rules below were written with their letters lined up on purpose.

chain a-killer-confesses + the-priest-sets-a-penance within 8:
  {1.A} could not carry it alone, and told {1.P} what {1.A:he} had done to {1.C}; {2.P} heard {2.A:him}
  out, and laid a penance on {2.A:him} that had {2.Q'} at the end of it.

chain a-killer-confesses + the-priest-tells-the-son + blood-for-blood within 60:
  {1.A} confessed the killing of {1.C} to {1.P} under the seal; {2.P}, who should have carried it to
  {2.P:his} own grave, let {2.X} know whose hand it had been, and {3.X} swore that {3.A} would answer
  for {3.C:his} {3.C:father}'s death.

chain a-killer-confesses + the-priest-tells-the-son within 60:
  {1.A} confessed the killing of {1.C} to {1.P} under the seal, and {2.P}, who should have carried it
  to {2.P:his} own grave, let {2.X} know whose hand it had been.

chain the-priest-tells-the-son + blood-for-blood within 10:
  It was from {1.P}, who had it under the seal, that {1.X} learned it was {1.A} who killed {1.C}, and
  {2.X} swore as a son must that {2.A} would answer for it.

chain a-penitent-gives-up-his-plot + the-penance-is-done within 70:
  {1.A}, with a penance to serve, put aside whatever {1.A:he} had meant to do to {1.B}; when the time
  was served {2.A} was absolved, and the thing was never spoken of again.

chain the-son-looks-for-someone-to-blame + the-suspicion-is-said-aloud within 16:
  {1.X}, with a grave to stand at and nobody to lay it against, settled on {1.B} for no better reason
  than that {1.B} was there, and before long was saying so where the village could hear it.

chain a-widow-suspects-the-other-house + the-suspicion-is-said-aloud within 16:
  {1.X} had no doubt where to look for {1.C}'s death, and said the name of {1.B} aloud, with the
  houses already at each other and nothing but that to go on.

chain suspicion-falls-on-the-other-house + the-suspicion-is-said-aloud within 16:
  {1.X} decided that {1.C}'s death lay at the door of the other house, and named {1.B} for it in
  front of the village.

chain the-suspicion-is-said-aloud + the-accused-strikes-back within 10:
  {1.X} named {1.B} for it where the whole village could hear, and {2.B}, who had done nothing,
  resolved that if {2.B:he} was to be hanged for a killing it might as well be one {2.B:he} had done.

chain the-suspicion-is-said-aloud + the-houses-fall-out-over-an-accusation within 8:
  {1.X} named {1.B} for it in front of the village, and the houses of {2.H} and {2.K}, at peace that
  morning, were not at peace by the evening.

chain the-suspicion-spreads + the-suspicion-is-said-aloud within 12:
  What {1.X} thought of {1.B} had got as far as {1.Y} by then, and it was not long before somebody
  said it out loud.

chain a-hard-season + the-head-borrows within 16:
  The season went badly for the house of {1.H}, and {2.F} went to {2.G} for silver, with {2.D'} set
  on the note.

chain the-head-borrows + the-note-comes-due within 45:
  {1.F} had gone to {1.G} for silver against {1.D'}, and when the day came there was nothing to meet
  it with: the house of {1.H} was ruined.

chain the-note-comes-due + a-ruined-man-turns-on-his-creditor within 12:
  The note came due and {1.F} could not meet it; ruined, {2.F} began to think that {2.G} would be
  easier to be rid of than to pay.

chain the-note-comes-due + a-ruined-house-marries-down within 20:
  {1.F} could not meet the note, and with the house ruined {2.A} was promised to {2.B} on terms
  nobody pretended were good, the wedding set for {2.M'}.

# --- chains among the older arcs ----------------------------------------------
#
# Three firings told as one sentence is the longest thing the narrator makes,
# and a plot that is found out and turned around is exactly that shape.

chain the-plotter-finds-an-accomplice + the-accomplice-turns + the-warned-strike-first within 10:
  {1.C} found {1.X}, who had no love for {1.B}, willing to help; {2.X} lost {2.X:his} nerve before it
  came to anything and told {2.B} what was intended, and {3.B}, forewarned, resolved to be the first
  to move.

chain the-plotter-finds-an-accomplice + a-friend-warns-his-friend within 10:
  {1.C} found {1.X} willing to help against {1.B}, and it was {2.X}, who counted {2.B} a friend, who
  could not go through with it and said so.

chain the-widow-learns-who-killed-him + the-witness-asks-for-silence within 10:
  {1.B} learned it was {1.A} who had killed {1.C}, and rather than take it to anyone else, named a
  price for keeping it quiet.

chain the-heads-make-a-match + she-runs-off-with-her-lover within 80:
  {1.F} and {1.G} came to terms and {1.A} was promised to {1.B}, and for all the terms they came to,
  {2.A} ran off with {2.X} and married him instead, and the houses have not spoken since.

# --- one sentence per rule ---------------------------------------------------

the-feeling-is-returned: {B} came to return {A}'s affection.

the-esteem-is-returned: {A} and {B} became friends.
a-friend-turns-on-a-killer: {X} would not call a killer of {C} a friend, and turned on {A}.
