a-friend-avenges-a-friend: {X} swore that {A} would answer for {C}'s death, as a friend should.

a-thin-wall: {A} heard {C} through the wall, and knew what {C:he} intended.
the-eavesdropper-warns-the-victim: {A}, who had heard it all through the wall, told {B} what {C} intended.
the-plotter-learns-he-was-heard: {C} learned that {A} had been listening.
the-eavesdropper-denounces-a-traitor: {A} carried what {A:he} had heard to the king: {C} had designs on {K}.

