hatred-fades: {A} let {A:his} grudge against {B} go.

they-get-engaged: {A} and {B} were engaged.
they-set-a-date: {A} and {B} set their wedding for {D'}.
they-take-their-time: {A} and {B}, in no great hurry, set their wedding for {D'}.
they-wait-for-a-better-season: {A} and {B} would wait for a better season, and set their wedding for {D'}.
the-vows-are-said: {A} and {B} were married at {C}.
the-betrothed-mourns: The wedding of {B} and {A}, set for {D}, never took place.
the-engagement-dies-with-him: {B}'s engagement to {A} died with {A:him}.

the-heads-make-a-match: {F} and {G} came to terms: {A} was promised to {B}, to be wed in {D'}.
