the-jilted-man-plots-against-the-lover: {B}, jilted, resolved that {X} would not have {A} for long.
the-jilted-woman-plots-against-the-lover: {B}, jilted, resolved that {X} would not have {A} for long.
the-jilted-nurse-a-grudge: {B} never forgave {A}.
the-jilted-let-it-go: {B} put {A} out of {B:his} mind.

the-feud-claims-a-target: With the houses at feud, {B} marked {Y} for death.
the-feud-burns-out: The feud between {K} and {H} burned itself out.

he-plots-against-the-groom: {C}, wanting {A}, resolved that {B} would not live to see {D}.
she-plots-against-the-bride: {C}, wanting {A}, resolved that {B} would not live to see {D}.
he-covets-another-mans-wife: {A} wanted {B}, and began to think how {C} might be got out of the way.
she-covets-another-womans-husband: {A} wanted {B}, and began to think how {C} might be got out of the way.

the-plotter-finds-an-accomplice: {C} found {X}, who had no love for {B}, willing to help.
a-lover-is-drawn-into-the-plot: {X}, for love of {C}, was drawn into it.
the-accomplice-turns: {X} lost {X:his} nerve and warned {B} what {C} intended.
the-betrayed-man-learns-of-it: {C} learned it was {X} who had talked.
the-warned-strike-first: Forewarned, {B} resolved to strike at {C} first.
the-warned-keep-their-guard: {B} kept {B:his} guard up, and let it be.

poison: {C} began putting poison in {B}'s food.
released:poison: {B} died; it was {C}'s poison.
cancel:poison: {B} was spared the poison.
a-knife-in-the-dark: {C} waited for {B} in the dark with a knife.
