the-plot-comes-to-nothing: {C} thought better of it.
the-moment-passes: The day came and went, and {C}'s plot against {B} came to nothing.

blood-for-blood: {X} swore that {A} would answer for {X:his} {C:father}'s death.
a-father-avenges-his-son: {X} swore that {A} would answer for {X:his} {C:son}'s death.
the-widow-swears-vengeance: {B}, widowed by {A}'s hand, swore {A} would pay for it.
a-kinsman-takes-up-the-blood-debt: {X}, of {C}'s house, took up the blood-debt against {A}.
the-killing-goes-unavenged: Nobody took up {C}'s cause.
the-widow-learns-who-killed-him: {B} learned it was {A} who had killed {C}, and came to hate {A:him}.

she-conceives: {A} was found to be with child.
a-child-is-born: {A} bore {B} a {C':son}, whom they named {C'}.
she-dies-in-childbed: {A} died in childbed, and the child with her.
